{
  "title": "Single Number II",
  "description": "In the list `nums`, every value appears **exactly three times** except for one value that appears exactly once. Return that value.\n\n### Examples\n\n| `nums` | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `[2, 2, 3, 2]` | `3` |\n| `[0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 99]` | `99` |\n| `[-2, -2, 1, -2]` | `1` |\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `1 <= nums.size() <= 1000`\n- `-2^31 <= nums[i] <= 2^31 - 1`\n- Try to use constant extra memory.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "int single_number_ii(vector<int> nums) {\n    unsigned int result = 0;\n    for (int bit = 0; bit < 32; ++bit) {\n        int count = 0;\n        for (int x : nums) {\n            count += (static_cast<unsigned int>(x) >> bit) & 1u;\n        }\n        if (count % 3 != 0) {\n            result |= 1u << bit;\n        }\n    }\n    return static_cast<int>(result);\n}\n",
  "template": "int single_number_ii(vector<int> nums) {\n    // Return the one value that does not appear three times.\n    return 0;\n}\n",
